course: dictionary
lesson: 3418
title: Many meanings of expression
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Toad sat in the middle of the dusty road ... his face wore a placid satisfied expression.» Here expression is the look on Toad's face. Placid is a clue: a placid face is calm, so the expression shows his calm, happy feelings.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «He sang it very loud, with great unction and expression.» Expression here means feeling put into the singing. In reading lessons, «read with expression» means reading with feeling, not just saying the words.
explain: Always check the words around the word. Read the sentence, guess the meaning, then swap your meaning in and see if it still makes sense. In maths, an expression is a group of numbers and signs, and it has no equals sign.
fact: Expression can mean a word or phrase with a special meaning, like a saying.
fact: The look on a person's face that shows feeling is an expression.
fact: In maths, an expression is a group of numbers, letters and signs, such as 3 + 4, with no equals sign.
fact: «Placid» means calm, so a placid expression is a calm look.
fact: Roots ending in ss take -ssion: express becomes expression, and discuss becomes discussion.
exercise: «Toad's face wore a placid satisfied expression.» What does expression mean here? | A long sentence about a road | Reading with feeling in a book | *The look on his face that shows how he feels | A sum with numbers and signs
exercise: In maths, 3 + 4 is called an expression. Why? | It is a word from a story | *It is a group of numbers and signs with no equals sign | It has an equals sign in it | It is always a single letter
exercise: «He sang it very loud, with great unction and expression.» Find and copy one word that means calm or feeling. | sang | with | loud | *expression
test: In Quebec, «C'est l'fun!» means what? | Look out! | Where is the fun? | *It's fun! | Good morning, how are you?
test: In the phrase «read with expression», expression means what? | Reading very fast | *Reading with feeling | Reading in a quiet room | A word that rhymes with reading
exam: The root express takes which ending to make the noun? | -ment | -ness | *-ssion | -tion
